Z||000017||Pontiaddict||09-13-2000||02:17 PM||||How about this, Instead of running the scoops over the roof, how about running them over the sides of the notchback?<P>Or you can do the PISA fastback conversion ( <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com/mnfr/fierohq/gtfx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cybercars.com/mnfr/fierohq/gtfx.html</A>  ). Then add the aftermarket quarter window replacements ( <A HREF="http://members.yourlink.net/wclw/fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.yourlink.net/wclw/fiero.htm</A>  ).<BR>Then, add some panels to the inside of the fastback that travel the length of the fastback and route the air into the engine compartment.<P>The scoos and the fastback together run about a grand though.<P>Bella, post pics when you can. I've been wondering what your car looks like since the first time you described the changes to it.<P>||||reg||1
