Z||000020||ThatRickGuy||09-14-2000||10:12 AM||||There's been some talk about the Fi-Air-O sccops not being functional. I would say that they would not be functional for certain uses. True, pushing air into the engine bay from the top &gt;may&lt; cause a higher preasure under the back of the car, but that's not the only way to use them. If you installed enlarged scoops (PISA, or the 3 piece ones are my favorites) on either side, but left the inside open (use them just as cool air intakes) Then mounted the Fi-Air-O intakes, and plumbed them to work with Chris West's dual throttle body intake like a ram air system. And top the hood off with a rearward facing scoop (I think the one DXR Dad &lt;?&gt; was using was what I was thinking) add in the Fiero Shop's front hood scoops, and you should be able to keep the temps down and have functional dual intake ram air. Now if I just had a couple of grand to do it with  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
